/-!
# The exterior power of a unipotent endomorphism, modulo the first step of the wedge filtration

Let `0 ⟶ ℱ --iF--> ℋ ⟶ 𝒢 ⟶ 0` be a locally split short exact sequence of sheaves of modules on a
space. Two splittings of it differ by the unipotent automorphism

`θ = 𝟙 - g ≫ (sp.s ≫ sp'.r) ≫ iF`

of `ℋ` (`CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.Splitting.transition`), and the two local Künneth
comparisons `⨁_{p + q = n}(⋀ᵖℱ ⊗ ⋀^q𝒢) ⟶ ⋀ⁿℋ` attached to the two splittings differ by
postcomposition with `⋀ⁿθ` and by nothing else
(`SheafOfModules.exteriorPowerProdHom_eq_of_comp`). **This file proves that `⋀ⁿθ` is the
identity modulo the first step of the wedge filtration**, so that the two comparisons agree on
the graded pieces: for `n = 1 + k` the difference `⋀ⁿθ - 𝟙` dies against the cokernel of

`⋀¹ℱ ⊗ ⋀^{k}ℋ ⟶ ⋀^{1+k}ℋ`,

the wedge-product component morphism `SheafOfModules.prodWedgeHom` taken along `iF` and the
identity of `ℋ`. That image is the first step `F¹` of the filtration of Section 50.12, written
out directly rather than through any packaging of the filtration, so that this statement
composes with any of them.

The hypothesis on `θ` is only that it is `𝟙 + w ≫ iF` for *some* `w : ℋ ⟶ ℱ`: nothing about `w`
is used, in particular not that it factors through `𝒢`.

## Main definitions

* `SheafOfModules.firstStepTotalIdeal`: the right ideal of the ungraded realization of `⋀ℋ`
  generated by the degree-one sections coming from `ℱ`. Its degree-`1 + k` component is `F¹` on
  sections.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ExteriorUnipotent.listProd_add_sub_mem`: **the multilinear expansion**, as an identity
  of products in a ring: a product of sums `∏(aᵢ + bᵢ)` agrees with `∏aᵢ` modulo any additive
  subgroup absorbing multiplication on the right which contains the `bᵢ`, provided the `bⱼ`
  anticommute with all the factors. This is `Stacks.ExteriorUnipotent.listProd_mul_eq_or_neg`,
  which moves an anticommuting factor across a product, applied to each term of the expansion.
* `Stacks.GradedAlgebra.genLin_mul_anticomm`: degree-one sections in the image of a square-zero
  generator anticommute in the ungraded realization — the exterior counterpart of
  `Stacks.GradedAlgebra.genLin_mul_comm`.
* `SheafOfModules.hom_eq_zero_of_homogeneousProd`: **a morphism out of `⋀ⁿℋ` which kills every
  wedge of local sections is zero.** This is what reduces a statement about `⋀ⁿθ` to the
  section-level computation, and it rests on the fact that germs of wedges span every stalk.
* `SheafOfModules.mem_range_prodWedgeHom_val_app_mul` and
  `SheafOfModules.proj_mem_range_of_mem_firstStepTotalIdeal`: **the section-level membership
  criterion for `F¹`**: a product of a degree-one section coming from `ℱ` with a degree-`k`
  section of `⋀ℋ` is a value of the component morphism, and hence so is the degree-`1 + k`
  component of any element of the right ideal those products generate.
* `SheafOfModules.exists_prodWedgeHom_val_app_eq_pieceMap_sub`: **the expansion of `⋀ⁿθ` on a
  wedge of local sections**, which is the mathematical heart of the file.
* `SheafOfModules.pieceMap_unipotent_sub_id_comp_cokernelπ` and
  `SheafOfModules.factors_imageSubobject_pieceMap_unipotent_sub_id`: **`⋀ⁿ` of a unipotent
  endomorphism is the identity modulo `F¹`**, in the cokernel form and in the image-subobject
  form.
* `SheafOfModules.pieceMap_transition_sub_id_comp_cokernelπ` and
  `SheafOfModules.exteriorPowerProdHom_splitting_sub_comp_cokernelπ`: the same statement at the
  transition automorphism of two splittings, and the consequence that **the two Künneth
  comparisons agree modulo `F¹`**, which is the step of Section 0FMK that identifies the graded
  pieces of the filtration.

## Implementation notes

**Why the ungraded realization.** The expansion of `θ(h₀) ∧ ⋯ ∧ θ(h_k)` needs associativity and
anticommutativity of the wedge product. In the graded algebra both are heterogeneous equalities
(`Stacks.GradedAlgebra.mul_assoc` is an `HEq`, because the two bracketings land in propositionally
but not definitionally equal degrees), whereas in the ungraded realization `Total` they are the
`Ring` structure's own `mul_assoc` and a two-line consequence of square-zero. The whole
computation is therefore carried out there, through `Stacks.GradedAlgebra.incl_homogeneousProd`,
and transported back by `Stacks.GradedAlgebra.proj_incl`: `incl` is injective with `proj` as a
left inverse, and `proj` in degree `1 + k` kills every other homogeneous component
(`Stacks.GradedAlgebra.proj_incl_of_ne`).

**Why a right ideal and not a two-sided one.** Modulo the two-sided ideal generated by the image
of `ℱ` the expansion is immediate, with no anticommutation needed; but the degree-`1 + k` part of
a two-sided ideal is not visibly the image of `⋀¹ℱ ⊗ ⋀^kℋ ⟶ ⋀^{1+k}ℋ`, since recognizing
`x · iF(c) · y` as a left multiple of `iF(c)` would need graded commutativity for *arbitrary*
homogeneous sections, which holds only locally. With the right ideal the degreewise statement is
exactly the membership criterion above, and the anticommutation is confined to
`Stacks.ExteriorUnipotent.listProd_mul_eq_or_neg`, where only images of degree-one generators
occur.

**Degrees are written `1 + k`.** `SheafOfModules.prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 ℋ) 1 k` lands in
`⋀^{1+k}ℋ`, and `((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ)` is definitionally `(1 : ℤ) + (k : ℤ)`, so no transport
appears anywhere. A consumer wanting the statement at a degree `n` presented as `k + 1` should
compose with `SheafOfModules.prodWedgeHomOfEq`, which is the library's transport.

**The abelian structure is a pinned local instance.** The cokernel and the image subobject are
taken in the abelian category of sheaves of modules; searching for that instance from
`SheafOfModules.instAbelian` exceeds the default instance-synthesis budget at these binders, so
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.abelianOfSmallSite` — the same instance, stated once with the
sheafification side conditions already discharged — is turned on with
`attribute [local instance]` in each section that needs it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FMK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FMK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01C6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01C6)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Sheaf CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite

/-! The wedge-product morphisms below go out of an object built by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor`, which is indexed by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf`, into one indexed by
`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat`. The two are the same bundled sheaf of rings, but `ringSheaf` is
an opaque `def`, so the abelian structure pinned below is not recognised at the first spelling
and the cokernels taken here lose their zero morphism. Making `ringSheaf` reducible for
implicit-argument unification identifies the two at no further cost. -/
attribute [local implicit_reducible] Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf

universe v u w a

/-! ### Products in a ring whose factors anticommute with a distinguished element -/

namespace Stacks.ExteriorUnipotent

variable {Rng : Type*} [Ring Rng]

/-- **Moving an anticommuting element across a product.** If `b` anticommutes with every entry of
a list, then moving `b` from the right of the product of that list to its left changes at most the
sign. The sign itself is `(-1)` to the length of the list, but only the disjunction is needed
below, and stating it that way keeps the parity bookkeeping out of the consumers. -/
theorem listProd_mul_eq_or_neg (b : Rng) (l : List Rng) (h : ∀ x ∈ l, x * b = -(b * x)) :
    l.prod * b = b * l.prod ∨ l.prod * b = -(b * l.prod) := by
  induction l with
  | nil => exact Or.inl (by rw [List.prod_nil, one_mul, mul_one])
  | cons x l ih =>
      have hx : x * b = -(b * x) := h x (List.mem_cons_self ..)
      have hl : ∀ y ∈ l, y * b = -(b * y) := fun y hy => h y (List.mem_cons_of_mem _ hy)
      rw [List.prod_cons, mul_assoc]
      rcases ih hl with hc | hc
      · rw [hc, ← mul_assoc, hx, neg_mul, mul_assoc]
        exact Or.inr rfl
      · rw [hc, mul_neg, ← mul_assoc, hx, neg_mul, neg_neg, mul_assoc]
        exact Or.inl rfl

/-- A product all of whose factors anticommute with an element `b` of a right ideal `S` again
lies in `S` when `b` is multiplied in on the right: by
`Stacks.ExteriorUnipotent.listProd_mul_eq_or_neg` the product is `±b` times the product, and `S`
absorbs multiplication on the right. -/
theorem listProd_mul_mem (S : AddSubgroup Rng) (hS : ∀ y ∈ S, ∀ z : Rng, y * z ∈ S)
    (b : Rng) (hb : b ∈ S) (l : List Rng) (h : ∀ x ∈ l, x * b = -(b * x)) :
    l.prod * b ∈ S := by
  rcases listProd_mul_eq_or_neg b l h with hc | hc
  · rw [hc]
    exact hS b hb _
  · rw [hc]
    exact neg_mem (hS b hb _)

/-- **The expansion of a product of sums, modulo a right ideal containing the perturbations.**
Let `S` be an additive subgroup of a ring absorbing multiplication on the right, let `b₀, …,
b_{n-1}` be elements of `S` and `a₀, …, a_{n-1}` arbitrary, and suppose all the `aᵢ` and `bⱼ`
anticommute with all the `bⱼ`. Then

`(a₀ + b₀) ⋯ (a_{n-1} + b_{n-1}) ≡ a₀ ⋯ a_{n-1}` modulo `S`.

Every term of the multilinear expansion other than the one with no perturbation has a factor
`bⱼ`, which the anticommutation moves to the left of the term. -/
theorem listProd_add_sub_mem (S : AddSubgroup Rng) (hS : ∀ y ∈ S, ∀ z : Rng, y * z ∈ S) :
    ∀ (n : ℕ) (a b : Fin n → Rng), (∀ i, b i ∈ S) →
      (∀ i j, a i * b j = -(b j * a i)) → (∀ i j, b i * b j = -(b j * b i)) →
      (List.ofFn fun i => a i + b i).prod - (List.ofFn fun i => a i).prod ∈ S := by
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero =>
      intro a b _ _ _
      simp
  | succ n ih =>
      intro a b hb hab hbb
      rw [List.ofFn_succ', List.concat_eq_append, List.prod_append, List.prod_singleton,
        List.ofFn_succ', List.concat_eq_append, List.prod_append, List.prod_singleton]
      have hE := ih (fun i => a i.castSucc) (fun i => b i.castSucc) (fun i => hb _)
        (fun i j => hab _ _) (fun i j => hbb _ _)
      have hanti : ∀ x ∈ (List.ofFn fun i : Fin n => a i.castSucc + b i.castSucc),
          x * b (Fin.last n) = -(b (Fin.last n) * x) := by
        intro x hx
        rw [List.mem_ofFn] at hx
        obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := hx
        rw [add_mul, mul_add, hab, hbb, neg_add]
      have key := AddSubgroup.add_mem S (hS _ hE (a (Fin.last n)))
        (listProd_mul_mem S hS (b (Fin.last n)) (hb _) _ hanti)
      have heq : ((List.ofFn fun i : Fin n => a i.castSucc + b i.castSucc).prod -
            (List.ofFn fun i : Fin n => a i.castSucc).prod) * a (Fin.last n) +
          (List.ofFn fun i : Fin n => a i.castSucc + b i.castSucc).prod * b (Fin.last n) =
          (List.ofFn fun i : Fin n => a i.castSucc + b i.castSucc).prod *
              (a (Fin.last n) + b (Fin.last n)) -
            (List.ofFn fun i : Fin n => a i.castSucc).prod * a (Fin.last n) := by
        noncomm_ring
      rwa [heq] at key

end Stacks.ExteriorUnipotent

/-! ### Degree-one generators of an exterior algebra anticommute -/

namespace Stacks.GradedAlgebra

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {O : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{w}}
  {Pc : ℤ → PresheafOfModules.{max w a} (O ⋙ forget₂ _ RingCat)}
  (A : Stacks.GradedAlgebra Pc) {F : PresheafOfModules.{max w a} (O ⋙ forget₂ _ RingCat)}
  (gen : F ⟶ Pc 1)

/-- **Degree-one sections in the image of a square-zero generator anticommute** in the ungraded
realization: `x · y = -(y · x)`. The generator is additive, so the square of the image of the sum
of two sections vanishes (`Stacks.GradedAlgebra.genLin_sq_zero`), and expanding that square
leaves exactly `x · y + y · x = 0`.

This is the exterior counterpart of `Stacks.GradedAlgebra.genLin_mul_comm`, which records that
the images of a *commuting* generator commute. -/
theorem genLin_mul_anticomm (hs : A.GenSquareZero gen) (X : Cᵒᵖ) (m m' : F.obj X) :
    A.genLin gen X m * A.genLin gen X m' = -(A.genLin gen X m' * A.genLin gen X m) := by
  have hsum := A.genLin_sq_zero gen hs X (m + m')
  rw [map_add, add_mul, mul_add, mul_add, A.genLin_sq_zero gen hs X m,
    A.genLin_sq_zero gen hs X m', zero_add, add_zero] at hsum
  exact eq_neg_of_add_eq_zero_left hsum

end Stacks.GradedAlgebra

/-! ### Morphisms out of an exterior power are determined on wedges of local sections -/

namespace SheafOfModules

section Vanishing

variable {X : TopCat.{u}} {Osharp : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) CommRingCat.{u}}
  {H Q : SheafOfModules.{u} (Sheaf.toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Osharp)}
  (A : TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) H)

/-- **A morphism out of an exterior power which kills every wedge of local sections is zero.**
Germs of wedges of local sections span every stalk of `⋀ⁿ H`
(`SheafOfModules.span_germWedgeSet_eq_top`), so the hypothesis forces every stalk map to vanish;
a section of a sheaf all of whose germs vanish is zero. -/
theorem hom_eq_zero_of_homogeneousProd (n : ℕ) (g : A.exteriorPower n ⟶ Q)
    (hg : ∀ (U : Opens ↥X) (h : Fin n → H.val.obj (op U)),
      g.val.app (op U) (A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd (op U) n
        fun i => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app (op U) (h i)) = 0) :
    g = 0 := by
  have hstalk : ∀ x : ↥X, PresheafOfModules.stalkMapL x g.val = 0 := by
    intro x
    refine LinearMap.ext_on (span_germWedgeSet_eq_top A n x) ?_
    rintro z ⟨V, hxV, s, rfl⟩
    rw [PresheafOfModules.stalkMapL_germ, hg V s, LinearMap.zero_apply]
    exact map_zero _
  refine SheafOfModules.hom_ext (PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun U => ?_)
  obtain ⟨U⟩ := U
  refine ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun t => ?_)
  refine TopCat.Presheaf.section_ext
    ((_root_.SheafOfModules.toSheaf (Sheaf.toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Osharp)).obj Q)
    U (g.val.app (op U) t) 0 ?_
  intro x hx
  change TopCat.Presheaf.germ Q.val.presheaf U x hx (g.val.app (op U) t) =
    TopCat.Presheaf.germ Q.val.presheaf U x hx 0
  rw [← PresheafOfModules.stalkMapL_germ x g.val U hx t, hstalk x, LinearMap.zero_apply,
    map_zero]

end Vanishing

/-! ### The first step of the wedge filtration, on local sections -/

section Unipotent

variable {X : TopCat.{u}} {Osharp : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) CommRingCat.{u}}
  {F H : SheafOfModules.{u} (Sheaf.toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Osharp)}
  (AF : TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) F)
  (A : TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) H)

/-- **The section-level membership criterion for the first step of the wedge filtration.** A
product `(⋀¹iF)(c) · ξ` of a degree-one section coming from `F` with a degree-`k` section of
`⋀H` is a value of the wedge-product component morphism `⋀¹F ⊗ ⋀^k H ⟶ ⋀^{1+k}H`, namely its
value on the image of the pure tensor `c ⊗ ξ`: the component morphism is the tensor product of
`⋀¹iF` with `⋀^k𝟙 = 𝟙` followed by the multiplication of the exterior algebra of `H`.

The computation of the component morphism on a pure tensor of two arbitrary local sections is
the same one that
`SheafOfModules.prodWedgeHomIdRight_val_app_tensorSheafUnit` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DeRham.ExteriorPowerFiltration` performs in arbitrary bidegrees;
it is carried out inside this proof rather than restated, so that no declaration is duplicated.
What is stated here is the membership, which is what the sections below consume. -/
theorem mem_range_prodWedgeHom_val_app_mul (iF : F ⟶ H) (k : ℕ) (U : (Opens ↥X)ᵒᵖ)
    (c : (AF.exteriorPower 1).val.obj U) (ξ : (A.exteriorPower k).val.obj U) :
    (A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.mul (1 : ℤ) (k : ℤ)).app U
        ((AF.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.pieceMap A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra iF
          (1 : ℤ)).val.app U c) ξ ∈
      LinearMap.range ((prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k).val.app U).hom := by
  refine ⟨(PresheafOfModules.tensorSheafUnit (AF.exteriorPower 1) (A.exteriorPower k)).app U
    (c ⊗ₜ ξ), ?_⟩
  have hmap := Stacks.TensorSheafWorld.tensorSheafBifunctor_map_val_app_tensorSheafUnit
    Osharp (AF.exteriorPower 1) (A.exteriorPower k)
    (AF.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.pieceMap A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra iF (1 : ℤ))
    (A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.pieceMap A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra (𝟙 H) (k : ℤ)) U c ξ
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg
    (fun z => (GradedAlgebra.mulSheaf A.exterior (1 : ℤ) (k : ℤ)).val.app U z) hmap) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (GradedAlgebra.mulSheaf_unit A.exterior (1 : ℤ) (k : ℤ) U _ _) ?_
  rw [GradedAlgebra.IsExteriorAlgebra.pieceMap_id]
  rfl

/-- **The right ideal of the ungraded realization of `⋀H` generated by the degree-one sections
coming from `F`**, for a morphism `iF : F ⟶ H`: the additive subgroup generated by the products
`(⋀¹iF)(c) · u`. Its degree-`1 + k` part is the first step of the wedge filtration
(`SheafOfModules.proj_mem_range_of_mem_firstStepTotalIdeal`), and it is where the
non-identity terms of the expansion of a unipotent exterior power live. -/
def firstStepTotalIdeal (iF : F ⟶ H) (U : (Opens ↥X)ᵒᵖ) :
    AddSubgroup (A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.Total U) :=
  AddSubgroup.closure {y | ∃ (c : (AF.exteriorPower 1).val.obj U)
      (u : A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.Total U),
    y = A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl 1
        ((AF.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.pieceMap A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra iF
          (1 : ℤ)).val.app U c) * u}

/-- The ideal of `SheafOfModules.firstStepTotalIdeal` absorbs multiplication on the right: the
generators do, by associativity, and right multiplication by a fixed section is additive. -/
theorem mul_mem_firstStepTotalIdeal (iF : F ⟶ H) (U : (Opens ↥X)ᵒᵖ) :
    ∀ y ∈ firstStepTotalIdeal AF A iF U,
      ∀ u : A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.Total U, y * u ∈ firstStepTotalIdeal AF A iF U := by
  intro y hy u
  refine (AddSubgroup.closure_le
    (.comap (AddMonoidHom.mulRight u) (firstStepTotalIdeal AF A iF U))).2 ?_ hy
  rintro p ⟨c, u', rfl⟩
  refine AddSubgroup.mem_comap.2 ?_
  change A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl 1 _ * u' * u ∈ firstStepTotalIdeal AF A iF U
  rw [mul_assoc]
  exact AddSubgroup.subset_closure ⟨c, u' * u, rfl⟩

/-- A degree-one generator of `⋀H` attached to a local section coming from `F` lies in the ideal
of `SheafOfModules.firstStepTotalIdeal`: it is the image of the corresponding generator of `⋀¹F`
under `⋀¹iF`, times the unit. -/
theorem incl_generator_mem_firstStepTotalIdeal (iF : F ⟶ H) (U : (Opens ↥X)ᵒᵖ)
    (c : F.val.obj U) :
    A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl 1
        (A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U (iF.val.app U c)) ∈ firstStepTotalIdeal AF A iF U := by
  refine AddSubgroup.subset_closure ⟨AF.exteriorGenerator.val.app U c, 1, ?_⟩
  rw [mul_one]
  exact congrArg (A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl 1)
    (congrArg (fun m : F ⟶ A.exterior.piece 1 => m.val.app U c)
      (AF.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.map_app_one A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra iF).symm)

/-- **The degree-`1 + k` part of the ideal of `SheafOfModules.firstStepTotalIdeal` is the first
step of the wedge filtration**: the component in that degree of any element of the ideal is in
the image of the wedge-product component morphism `⋀¹F ⊗ ⋀^k H ⟶ ⋀^{1+k}H` on sections. A
generator `(⋀¹iF)(c) · u` contributes, after decomposing `u` into homogeneous pieces, only
through the degree-`k` piece, and there it is exactly the value of that morphism on a pure
tensor (`SheafOfModules.mem_range_prodWedgeHom_val_app_mul`). -/
theorem proj_mem_range_of_mem_firstStepTotalIdeal (iF : F ⟶ H) (k : ℕ) (U : (Opens ↥X)ᵒᵖ)
    (z : A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.Total U)
    (hz : z ∈ firstStepTotalIdeal AF A iF U) :
    A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.proj U ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ) z ∈
      LinearMap.range ((prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k).val.app U).hom := by
  have hle : firstStepTotalIdeal AF A iF U ≤
      AddSubgroup.comap (A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.proj U ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ)).toAddMonoidHom
        (LinearMap.range ((prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k).val.app U).hom).toAddSubgroup := by
    refine (AddSubgroup.closure_le _).2 ?_
    rintro p ⟨c, u, rfl⟩
    refine AddSubgroup.mem_comap.2 ?_
    change A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.proj U ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ)
        (A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl 1 _ * u) ∈
      LinearMap.range ((prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k).val.app U).hom
    induction u using A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl_induction with
    | zero =>
        rw [mul_zero, map_zero]
        exact Submodule.zero_mem _
    | incl m ym =>
        rw [A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl_mul_incl]
        by_cases hm : m = (k : ℤ)
        · subst hm
          have hpi : A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.proj U ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ)
                (A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl ((1 : ℤ) + (k : ℤ))
                  ((A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.mul (1 : ℤ) (k : ℤ)).app U
                    ((AF.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.pieceMap A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra iF
                      (1 : ℤ)).val.app U c) ym)) =
              (A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.mul (1 : ℤ) (k : ℤ)).app U
                ((AF.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.pieceMap A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra iF
                  (1 : ℤ)).val.app U c) ym :=
            A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.proj_incl U _ _
          rw [hpi]
          exact mem_range_prodWedgeHom_val_app_mul AF A iF k U c ym
        · rw [A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.proj_incl_of_ne U
            (show (1 : ℤ) + m ≠ ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ) by push_cast; omega)]
          exact Submodule.zero_mem _
    | add u₁ u₂ h₁ h₂ =>
        rw [mul_add, map_add]
        exact Submodule.add_mem _ h₁ h₂
  exact AddSubgroup.mem_comap.1 (hle hz)

/-- **The exterior power of a unipotent endomorphism is the identity on a wedge of local
sections, modulo the first step of the wedge filtration.** For `θ = 𝟙 + w ≫ iF` the difference
`⋀^{1+k}θ(s₀ ∧ ⋯ ∧ s_k) - s₀ ∧ ⋯ ∧ s_k` is a value of the wedge-product component morphism
`⋀¹F ⊗ ⋀^k H ⟶ ⋀^{1+k}H`.

The proof is the multilinear expansion of the product `θ(s₀) ⋯ θ(s_k)`, carried out in the
ungraded realization of the exterior algebra of `H`, where it is an identity between products in
a ring: every factor is `generator(sᵢ) + generator(iF(w(sᵢ)))`, so every term of the expansion
other than `s₀ ∧ ⋯ ∧ s_k` has a factor coming from `F`, and the anticommutation of degree-one
generators moves that factor to the front
(`Stacks.ExteriorUnipotent.listProd_add_sub_mem`). The resulting element of the right ideal
`SheafOfModules.firstStepTotalIdeal` is homogeneous of degree `1 + k`, where that ideal is the
image of the component morphism. -/
theorem exists_prodWedgeHom_val_app_eq_pieceMap_sub (iF : F ⟶ H) (w : H ⟶ F) (k : ℕ)
    (U : (Opens ↥X)ᵒᵖ) (s : Fin (1 + k) → H.val.obj U) :
    ∃ z, (prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k).val.app U z =
      (A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.pieceMap A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra (𝟙 H + w ≫ iF)
            ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ)).val.app U
          (A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd U (1 + k)
            fun i => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U (s i)) -
        A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd U (1 + k)
          fun i => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U (s i) := by
  have hθ : ∀ i, A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U ((𝟙 H + w ≫ iF).val.app U (s i)) =
      A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U (s i) +
        A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U (iF.val.app U (w.val.app U (s i))) := by
    intro i
    have h1 : (𝟙 H + w ≫ iF).val.app U (s i) = s i + iF.val.app U (w.val.app U (s i)) := rfl
    rw [h1, map_add]
  have hinclsub : ∀ x y : (A.exterior.piece ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ)).val.obj U,
      A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ) (x - y) =
        A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ) x -
          A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ) y := by
    intro x y
    refine eq_sub_of_add_eq ?_
    rw [← A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl_add]
    congr 1
    abel
  have hpm : A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.pieceMap A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra (𝟙 H + w ≫ iF)
        ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ) =
      (A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.map A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra
        (𝟙 H + w ≫ iF)).app ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ) := rfl
  have hanti := Stacks.GradedAlgebra.genLin_mul_anticomm A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra
    A.exteriorGenerator.val A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.1 U
  have hexp := Stacks.ExteriorUnipotent.listProd_add_sub_mem
    (firstStepTotalIdeal AF A iF U) (mul_mem_firstStepTotalIdeal AF A iF U) (1 + k)
    (fun i => A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl 1 (A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U (s i)))
    (fun i => A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl 1
      (A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U (iF.val.app U (w.val.app U (s i)))))
    (fun i => incl_generator_mem_firstStepTotalIdeal AF A iF U _)
    (fun _ _ => hanti _ _) (fun _ _ => hanti _ _)
  have hmem : A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ)
      ((A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.pieceMap A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra (𝟙 H + w ≫ iF)
            ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ)).val.app U
          (A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd U (1 + k)
            fun i => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U (s i)) -
        A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd U (1 + k)
          fun i => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U (s i)) ∈
      firstStepTotalIdeal AF A iF U := by
    rw [hinclsub, hpm,
      GradedAlgebra.UnitalHom.app_homogeneousProd_comp
        (A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.map A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra (𝟙 H + w ≫ iF))
        (𝟙 H + w ≫ iF)
        (A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.map_app_one A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra (𝟙 H + w ≫ iF))
        U (1 + k) s,
      A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl_homogeneousProd,
      A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.incl_homogeneousProd]
    simpa only [hθ, Stacks.GradedAlgebra.incl_add] using hexp
  have h2 := proj_mem_range_of_mem_firstStepTotalIdeal AF A iF k U _ hmem
  rw [A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.proj_incl] at h2
  exact h2

/-! Sheaves of modules over the base ring sheaf form an abelian category, which is what the
cokernel and the image subobject below are taken in. The instance is pinned rather than
restated: searching for it from `SheafOfModules.instAbelian` exceeds the default
instance-synthesis budget at these binders, and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.abelianOfSmallSite` is
that instance with the budget already spent. -/
attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafOfModules.abelianOfSmallSite

/-- **`⋀^n` of a unipotent endomorphism is the identity modulo the first step of the wedge
filtration.** Write `n = 1 + k`, let `iF : F ⟶ H` be a morphism of sheaves of modules and
`w : H ⟶ F` arbitrary, and let `θ = 𝟙 + w ≫ iF`, the general shape of an endomorphism of `H`
differing from the identity by a morphism factoring through `iF`. Then `⋀ⁿθ - 𝟙` vanishes after
composing with the cokernel of the wedge-product component morphism
`⋀¹F ⊗ ⋀^{n-1}H ⟶ ⋀ⁿH`, i.e. it factors through the image of that morphism
(`SheafOfModules.factors_imageSubobject_pieceMap_unipotent_sub_id`).

This is the statement the identification of the graded pieces of the filtration of Section 0FMK
rests on: the transition automorphism between two splittings of the transitivity sequence is of
this shape (`CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.Splitting.transition_sub_id`), the two local Künneth
comparisons differ by `⋀ⁿ` of it, and therefore induce the same map into the quotient by the
first step of the filtration. -/
theorem pieceMap_unipotent_sub_id_comp_cokernelπ (iF : F ⟶ H) (w : H ⟶ F) (k : ℕ) :
    (A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.pieceMap A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra (𝟙 H + w ≫ iF)
          ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ) - 𝟙 (A.exteriorPower (1 + k))) ≫
        Limits.cokernel.π (prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k) = 0 := by
  refine hom_eq_zero_of_homogeneousProd A (1 + k) _ fun V s => ?_
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := exists_prodWedgeHom_val_app_eq_pieceMap_sub AF A iF w k (op V) s
  have h1 : ((A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.pieceMap A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra (𝟙 H + w ≫ iF)
            ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ) - 𝟙 (A.exteriorPower (1 + k))) ≫
          Limits.cokernel.π (prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k)).val.app (op V)
        (A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd (op V) (1 + k)
          fun i => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app (op V) (s i)) =
      (Limits.cokernel.π (prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k)).val.app (op V)
        ((A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.pieceMap A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra (𝟙 H + w ≫ iF)
              ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ)).val.app (op V)
            (A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd (op V) (1 + k)
              fun i => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app (op V) (s i)) -
          A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd (op V) (1 + k)
            fun i => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app (op V) (s i)) := rfl
  rw [h1, ← hz]
  have h2 : (Limits.cokernel.π (prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k)).val.app (op V)
        ((prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k).val.app (op V) z) =
      (prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k ≫
        Limits.cokernel.π (prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k)).val.app (op V) z := rfl
  rw [h2, Limits.cokernel.condition]
  rfl

/-- **`⋀ⁿ` of a unipotent endomorphism factors as the identity plus a morphism through the first
step of the wedge filtration**: the subobject form of
`SheafOfModules.pieceMap_unipotent_sub_id_comp_cokernelπ`. The first step is written out as the
image subobject of the wedge-product component morphism `⋀¹F ⊗ ⋀^{n-1}H ⟶ ⋀ⁿH`, so that it does
not depend on any particular packaging of the filtration. -/
theorem factors_imageSubobject_pieceMap_unipotent_sub_id (iF : F ⟶ H) (w : H ⟶ F) (k : ℕ) :
    (Limits.imageSubobject (prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k)).Factors
      (A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.pieceMap A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra (𝟙 H + w ≫ iF)
        ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ) - 𝟙 (A.exteriorPower (1 + k))) := by
  have hexact : Limits.imageSubobject (prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k) =
      Limits.kernelSubobject (Limits.cokernel.π (prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k)) :=
    (ShortComplex.exact_iff_image_eq_kernel
      (ShortComplex.mk (prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k)
        (Limits.cokernel.π (prodWedgeHom AF A A iF (𝟙 H) 1 k))
        (Limits.cokernel.condition _))).1 (ShortComplex.exact_cokernel _)
  rw [hexact]
  exact Limits.kernelSubobject_factors _ _ (pieceMap_unipotent_sub_id_comp_cokernelπ AF A iF w k)

end Unipotent

/-! ### The transition automorphism between two splittings -/

section Transition

variable {X : TopCat.{u}} {Osharp : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) CommRingCat.{u}}
  {T : ShortComplex
    (SheafOfModules.{u} (Sheaf.toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Osharp))}
  (sp sp' : T.Splitting)
  (AF : TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) T.X₁)
  (AG : TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) T.X₃)
  (A : TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) T.X₂)

/-! The abelian structure, pinned as in the previous section. -/
attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafOfModules.abelianOfSmallSite

/-- **The exterior power of the transition automorphism of two splittings is the identity modulo
the first step of the wedge filtration.** For a short complex `0 ⟶ ℱ ⟶ ℋ ⟶ 𝒢 ⟶ 0` of sheaves of
modules with two splittings `sp`, `sp'`, the automorphism `θ` of `ℋ` carrying one to the other
(`CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.Splitting.transition`) differs from the identity by a morphism
factoring through `ℱ ⟶ ℋ` (`CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.Splitting.transition_sub_id`), so
`SheafOfModules.pieceMap_unipotent_sub_id_comp_cokernelπ` applies to it. -/
theorem pieceMap_transition_sub_id_comp_cokernelπ (k : ℕ) :
    (A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.pieceMap A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra (sp.transition sp')
          ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ) - 𝟙 (A.exteriorPower (1 + k))) ≫
        Limits.cokernel.π (prodWedgeHom AF A A T.f (𝟙 T.X₂) 1 k) = 0 := by
  have hθ : sp.transition sp' = 𝟙 T.X₂ + (-(T.g ≫ sp.s ≫ sp'.r)) ≫ T.f :=
    sub_eq_iff_eq_add'.1 (sp.transition_sub_id sp')
  rw [hθ]
  exact pieceMap_unipotent_sub_id_comp_cokernelπ AF A T.f _ k

/-- **The two Künneth comparisons attached to two splittings agree modulo the first step of the
wedge filtration.** The two comparisons

`⨁_{p + q = n} (⋀ᵖℱ ⊗ ⋀^q𝒢) ⟶ ⋀ⁿℋ`

differ by postcomposition with `⋀ⁿθ` for the transition automorphism `θ`
(`SheafOfModules.exteriorPowerProdHom_eq_of_comp`, since `θ` fixes `ℱ ⟶ ℋ` and carries `sp.s` to
`sp'.s`), and `⋀ⁿθ` is the identity modulo the image of `⋀¹ℱ ⊗ ⋀^{n-1}ℋ ⟶ ⋀ⁿℋ`. So the
composites of the two comparisons with the quotient by that image coincide: **the Künneth
decomposition of a graded piece does not depend on the chosen splitting.** This is the step of
Section 0FMK that identifies the graded pieces of the filtration. -/
theorem exteriorPowerProdHom_splitting_sub_comp_cokernelπ (k : ℕ) :
    (exteriorPowerProdHom AF AG A T.f sp'.s (1 + k) -
          exteriorPowerProdHom AF AG A T.f sp.s (1 + k)) ≫
        Limits.cokernel.π (prodWedgeHom AF A A T.f (𝟙 T.X₂) 1 k) = 0 := by
  have hsplit := exteriorPowerProdHom_eq_of_comp AF AG A A T.f sp.s (sp.transition sp') T.f sp'.s
    (sp.f_comp_transition sp') (sp.s_comp_transition sp') (1 + k)
  have hfac : exteriorPowerProdHom AF AG A T.f sp'.s (1 + k) -
        exteriorPowerProdHom AF AG A T.f sp.s (1 + k) =
      exteriorPowerProdHom AF AG A T.f sp.s (1 + k) ≫
        (A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra.pieceMap A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra (sp.transition sp')
          ((1 + k : ℕ) : ℤ) - 𝟙 (A.exteriorPower (1 + k))) := by
    rw [Preadditive.comp_sub, Category.comp_id]
    exact congrArg (fun z => z - exteriorPowerProdHom AF AG A T.f sp.s (1 + k)) hsplit
  rw [hfac, Category.assoc, pieceMap_transition_sub_id_comp_cokernelπ sp sp' AF A k, comp_zero]

end Transition

end SheafOfModules

end
